{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/938285-need-help-creating-a-totem-can-you-help-me","id":938285,"title":"Need Help creating a totem, can you help me ?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-07-27T12:56:01-07:00","id":938285,"title":"Need Help creating a totem, can you help me ?","content":"To make a long story short, im working on a totem creation for the pack of my players. Thing is, the Totem is a Rank 3 Fox spirit of perception and wisdom. Perception in all its forms is of course listening, looking, and the five sense, including the sixth sense, or intuition driven by instinct, and introspection needed to understand those things, hence the wisdom.<br /> <br /> Name: WatchFox the Wise.<br /> Rank 3 Spirit of Perception and wisdom.<br /> <br /> The two most influent members of the pack, by their play, presence, leadership and influence are 1 Iron Master, a cahalith, social worker type, and a Storm Lord Elodoth, wich operate as a private investigator.<br /> <br /> In the end, I have trouble with this:<br /> <br /> A Totem/Spirit needs Aspiration, Ban, and Bane.<br /> It is a real pain to find since so far, no one has actually come to any idea. <br /> <br /> Can you help me ? What would be your own idea on this ? Any input that could help us would be really fun to hear.<br /> <br /> Thanks.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T16:05:02-07:00","id":938410,"title":"","content":"Just checking a couple of things, I have some ideas but I want to be sure I've got everything lined up correctly.<br /> <br /> WatchFox the Wise is rank, 3, with an attribute pool of 15-25 for Rank 3 spirits, does your Pack have 12-22 points invested into Totem? (3 base points of attributes subtracted)<br /> <br /> Also, at least in my general understanding, foxes are generally known for Cunning, Stealth, Cowardice, Trickery. How does that play into WatchFox as a Spirit in regards to his trait, influences, general bio?<br /> <br /> Honestly, these are questions I'd pose to your Players, and have them help develop the character of WatchFox 'with' you. Personal opinion.<br /> <br /> As for an Aspiration, why has he become a Totem to the pack? What does he hope to gain from being tied to the Uratha? In general: what does he desire?<br /> <br /> Ban: I could go pretty simple here since you've got him focused on Perception and Wisdom. He cannot participate (could be changed to initiate) any confrontation (or fight) without knowing the name of his foe. Could be simpler or harder than that, just an idea for a baseline.<br /> <br /> Bane: One could go topical here, with the focus on misinformation and say: &quot;A periodical with a false headline for a story.&quot; Too many media sites put out bad information these days, whereas a newspaper with a story about the Girlscouts setting a local fundraising record wouldn't count.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12019-crimsonowl","name":"CrimsonOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-27T19:19:07-07:00","id":938501,"title":"","content":"Ok, I am back.<br /> <br /> I do not remember correctly how many points points the pack invested, but the 15-25 mark was easily reached. That is not a concern. They are around 18 or 19 I think.<br /> <br /> For some of your questions, my understanding is this:<br /> <br /> Fox are known to be clever and cunning, patient and can use trickery. Depending on culture, palces, and folklore fox may or may not cowards. Remeber that they are small and fragile, so they must be careful. They are survivors that use their mind to adapt. In Quebec, Canada, and in France, Fox are wise and clever. The legend of the Kitsune speak that with age, their powers and wisdom grow. Some legends see them as guardians able to see in both world. Some culture ties them to spirits and and understanding, and some native american culture see them as clever and wise, yet deceitful. Some fox adapt themselves to cities, and those urban foxes can hunt small stuff, and can scavenge. A private investigator, and a social worker tied to street working and darker side of our society do that... instead of looking for food in dumps, &quot;they look for information in dumps&quot;. <br /> <br /> In the end, an old fox with a survivor nature, adaptability nature, known for his clevernes, his cunning, his trickery, that is old enough to have seen everything, and survived, and not fall prey to any tricks since he is a trickster himself that knows every tricks in the book, is wise. Add to that the kutsune approach of power and wisdom... and you have it.<br /> <br /> Aspiration was for me to decide and I never did. At first, he was able to gain information about anything concerning the spirit world for example. &quot;Why there is a murdering spirit there ?&quot; Sometime he was asking the question, indirectly showing stuff to my player concerning their own environment... wich lead to some changes... and those change was a mutual benefits. Ex: Death and decay spirits are over there. My player got informed. Got there, found and half crazy vampire, fight, destroyed him, burned everything there, changing the landscape for good, wich had a positive impact on everyone. He is clever and wants to know and understand more. But he also wants to keep his &quot;hunting ground&quot; the more adequately fit for him.<br /> <br /> Ban: Thats a great idea. Since he his cautious, that would fit.<br /> Bane: Can you elaborate ? It is a great idea to put the journalism and flase stuff in here. One of the player is a independant journalist.<br /> <br /> Thank you <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T12:15:48-07:00","id":939012,"title":"","content":"I just wanted to double check the stats, sounds like you've got a hefty group and pack, I just wanted to make sure you didn't have like 3 people in the Pack and somehow they've got a Rank 3 Totem for some reason.<br /> <br /> I like your reply about Foxes, though, you did use Cunning at least a few times in there and definitely a few other traits that would probably relate more to Cunning than Wisdom. So I suppose my follow-up there is, in terms of development, if he's older and wiser, and say his Cunning was his Primary trait, is he at a point that his Wisdom has surpassed his Cunning, or is it still a secondary trait in comparison? Which of those aspects is winning out and how does that reflect on him as a spirit? Compare and apply nearly everything you've posted to say, a Raccoon, and I'd still probably call him Cunning primary, perhaps with some gained Wisdom. Just food for thought, trying to keep the gears turning and well oiled. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Glad you like the Ban, it could make for some really tough decisions depending on how you set things up. Good for pressure.<br /> <br /> So Banes are typically still something Physical, even for rank 2-3. I've got a sole-survivor character who still has his totem, but it is hardcore-weak. (4 points in Totem still only leaves the totem with 7 dots in attributes, total). Since the character had a drunk driver in his background and the totem is of Justice and Law, and Truth, his Bane is Alcohol; it clouds judgement and that's just unacceptable. When the group discovered an abandoned Speak-Easy underground, I pointed it out to the ST and simply had my character leave the area (at least to the outside). If my character's Totem came into contact with it, it'd be taking damage that could potentially destroy it.<br /> <br /> For Rank 2-3 based on the example they gave, I figured you needed something for WatchFox that could conceivably be readily available but that is also very specific. The image that came to mind for me was someone who'd figured out the bane, encircling him with bad tabloids, and rolling up a newspaper to fight him. A rolled up newspaper normally wouldn't do a whole lot except scold a dog, but in this case, it'd be a lethal form of attack.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":12019,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12019-crimsonowl","user":"CrimsonOwl","date":". 07-28-2016, 03:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12019-crimsonowl","name":"CrimsonOwl","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"20"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T15:54:33-07:00","id":939194,"title":"","content":"About the points:<br /> No no, my points are fine, 4 players in the pack with much investment, 2 of them (the 2 main players I was speaking about) that have 5 in Totem each. One private detective, One social Worker, one independant journalist, and one armorer, selling weapons and working in that said weapon store.<br /> Add some Wolf blood NPCs too with some of them with one dot investment. Its all great on that side.<br /> <br /> Concerning the Fox and the Wise approach:<br /> The reason I decided to use Wisdom is exactly that. The totem is an &quot;old and wise&quot; one. Besides, every fox are cunning. I mean, &quot;Fox the cunning one&quot; would be quite redundant. Or &quot;Bear the strong one&quot; would also be redundant since we already assume those quality. Giving a little more complexity with the fox, cleverness, and trickery, and we have a Wise one, the one that watch on many levels, and also understand on many levels. I was thinking about a hawk or an eagle, that would represent the perception easily, but it requires a more direct predatory approach, and is less likely to fit with my players and the &quot;wise&quot; part being reflexion and introspection. At the same time... introspection is a form of observation tied to perception itself. Ho well, I guess that you can addapt anything. Well, almost anything. Something like &quot;Small Pilchard the strong destroyer&quot; sounds... quite... weird.<br /> <br /> I like the Bane when you explain it like this. Thanks for the help !<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T22:01:31-07:00","id":939342,"title":"","content":"Some quick suggestions off the top of my head:<br /> <br /> <b>Aspirations</b><ul><li>To solve an unsolved mystery</li> <li>To find the hidden dens and Safe Places of its enemies.</li> <li>To outsmart its enemies</li> </ul><b>Bans</b><ul><li>WatchFox must treat peacefully with any who manage to sneak up on it</li> <li>WatchFox must perform a favour for any who have succesfully stumped it with a riddle.</li> </ul><b>Banes</b><ul><li>The natural weapons of any who knows its Ban.</li> <li>Weapons made from the bones of a fox that has been blinded.</li> <li>Weapons made from the bones of a fox that was caught in a trap.</li> </ul>Better ways to word some of those, and not really happy with any of the aspirations, but it's what I got.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":5279,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","user":"Amravanti","date":". 07-29-2016, 01:46 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T22:36:57-07:00","id":939354,"title":"","content":"Love those Banes, Amravanti! <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I must say, I thought that the first one was the natural weapons of any who know its Ban<b>e</b>, and I thought it was delightfully circuitous!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Freelance OPP. <b>Dark Eras</b>, <b>Shattered Dreams</b>, and counting!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2653-nated","name":"NateD","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2653_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"144"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T22:43:34-07:00","id":939359,"title":"","content":"Haha. That's so good I wish I'd thought of it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5279-amravanti","name":"Amravanti","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5279_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-07-28T23:48:42-07:00","id":939382,"title":"","content":"Well, guys, thanks alot.<br /> <br /> This is all very great and cool stuff.<br /> <br /> *Take notes !<br /> <br /> Seriously guys, you all did helped me alot !<br /> Thank you very much !","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2986-warriorshaman","name":"Warriorshaman","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"71"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}